/-!
# Descent of an admissible blowup along the completion of a Noetherian local ring

Let `A` be a Noetherian local ring and `B` its completion along the maximal ideal. An admissible
blowup of `Spec B`, relative to the punctured spectrum of `B`, is the base change of an admissible
blowup of `Spec A` relative to the punctured spectrum of `A`.

The centre of the given blowup is an ideal sheaf `J` on `Spec B` whose support misses the
punctured spectrum, so is contained in the closed point; by Noetherianity some power of the
maximal ideal of `B` lies in the corresponding ideal `K`, and such an ideal is generated by its
contraction to `A` (`Stacks.Blowup.ideal_map_comap_completion`). Mapping that contraction back
into the structure sheaf of `Spec A` produces the centre `C` downstairs, and the computation of
an inverse-image ideal sheaf on affines identifies `C.comap c` with `J`, where `c : Spec B ⟶
Spec A`. Since `A ⟶ B` is flat, blowing up commutes with the base change along `c`, which gives
the cartesian square.

## Main results

* `Stacks.Blowup.exists_isAdmissibleBlowup_isPullback_completion` is the descent: the admissible
  blowup downstairs, together with the cartesian square identifying the given blowup with its
  base change.

## Implementation notes

The ambient statement is about `Stacks.Blowup.IsAdmissibleBlowup`, whose isomorphism is to
`Stacks.Blowup.blowUp` — the blowup glued from the ordinary Rees algebras of the ideal on affine
opens. The universal property of blowing up, and hence the flat base change used here, is stated
for `AlgebraicGeometry.blowUp`, the relative `Proj` of the Rees algebra sheaf. The two are
identified over the base by `AlgebraicGeometry.blowUpIso` and
`AlgebraicGeometry.blowUpIso_hom_blowUpToBase`, and that identification is what lets the two
halves of the argument meet.

Flat base change for blowups (Stacks tag 0805) is used in the form
`AlgebraicGeometry.exists_isPullback_blowUpToBase_comap`, deduced from the universal property (tag
0806) exactly as the source does.

## References

* [Stacks Project, Tag 0AFK](https://stacks.math.columbia.edu/tag/0AFK)
* [Stacks Project, Tag 080K](https://stacks.math.columbia.edu/tag/080K)
* [Stacks Project, Tag 0805](https://stacks.math.columbia.edu/tag/0805)
-/

public section

open AlgebraicGeometry CategoryTheory CategoryTheory.Limits IsLocalRing

